course: dictionary
lesson: 16136
title: Wholehearted
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from two smaller words. Wholehearted is made from whole and heart. Together they help you picture the meaning: with all of your heart.
explain: The dictionary says wholehearted means completely sincere and enthusiastic, with no doubts. Sincere means you really mean it. Enthusiastic means keen and full of energy. So a wholehearted thank you is one that truly means it, with nothing held back.
explain: Use the clue words in the sentence. «The team gave wholehearted support to their captain.» Support means help, and wholehearted tells you that the help was full and keen, not half-hearted. To check, swap in "sincere and keen" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Wholehearted means completely sincere and enthusiastic, with no doubts.
fact: Wholehearted is an adjective, so it describes a noun, like «wholehearted support».
fact: Other phrases you may see are «wholehearted agreement» and «wholehearted thanks».
fact: In church, Christians speak of loving God wholeheartedly, which means loving Him with their whole heart.
fact: A wholehearted effort at school means giving everything you have, with no holding back.
exercise: «She gave her wholehearted effort to every task.» What does wholehearted effort mean? | Effort that someone else did for her | Effort that was only a little | *Effort given with all her heart, no holding back | Effort that she did while sleeping
exercise: «Our class gave a wholehearted cheer for the winning team.» What does wholehearted suggest about the cheer? | *Keen and full, with no doubts | Angry and rude | Tired and bored | Quiet and half-hearted
exercise: «Mum gave wholehearted agreement when I asked to go camping.» Your friend says wholehearted just means whole. Why is that not enough? | It means cut into pieces | It means the same as whole, nothing more | *It means she agreed fully and sincerely, with no doubts | It is a very long word
test: Which word is closest in meaning to wholehearted? | Careless | Doubtful | Unwilling | *Sincere
test: Which sentence shows a wholehearted apology? | I shrugged and said nothing at all | I said sorry while looking at my phone | I said sorry, but I hoped nobody heard | *I said sorry with my whole heart and I truly meant every word
exam: Which sentence uses wholehearted correctly? | *Our whole class gave wholehearted thanks to the nurse | The bus was wholehearted at noon | I wholehearted my dinner yesterday | Wholehearted is the name of a small bird
